]}, {"t": "XX", "lp": -0.00022097883629612625, "top": [["XX", -0.00022097883629612625], ["++", -9.238826751708984]]}, {"t": "_COMPILER", "lp": -0.0005945542361587286, "top": [["_COMPILER", -0.0005945542361587286], ["_compiler", -10.004788398742676]]}, {"t": "=", "lp": -0.0002593734534457326, "top": [["=", -0.0002593734534457326], [" ic", -10.531667709350586]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -3.993590871687047e-05, "top": [["ic", -3.993590871687047e-05], [" ic", -11.158483505249023]]}, {"t": "px", "lp": -0.00015844170411583036, "top": [["px", -0.00015844170411583036], ["PX", -10.7870454788208]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.000580002146307379, "top": [["`", -0.000580002146307379], [" `", -10.294572830200195]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` wouldn't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into confusing downstream errors.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag each part:\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` | **Source directory** \u2014 where the source code lives (the git clone). |\n| `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` | **Build directory** \u2014 where build artifacts go (out-of-source build). |\n| `-G Ninja` | Use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, efficient build system). |\n| `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` | Optimize build for **performance** (adds `-O3`, strips debug info). |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr` | Where `make install` will place files (system root). |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` | Put libraries in `lib/` (not `lib64/`). |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx` | Use Intel's **C compiler** (oneAPI DPC++/ICX). |\n| `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx`"}